SubHunter ("we," "our," or "us") is committed to protecting your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains how your information is collected, used, and disclosed by SubHunter.

This Privacy Policy applies to our application named SubHunter, and its associated subdomains (collectively, our "Service"). By accessing or using our Service, you signify that you have read, understood, and agree to our collection, storage, use, and disclosure of your personal information as described in this Privacy Policy and our Terms of Service.

1. Information We Collect
To provide you with the "painkiller" features of SubHunter—specifically tracking your subscriptions, calculating financial waste, and sending aggressive alerts—we may collect and process the following types of information:

A. Personal Data You Provide
When you use the app, you manually input specific data regarding your subscriptions. This includes:

Subscription Names: (e.g., Netflix, Spotify).

Financial Details: Costs, billing cycles, and renewal dates.

Preferences: Your settings regarding alert frequency and notification timing.

Note on Financial Data: The subscription data you input (names, costs, billing cycles and renewal dates) is stored in your account in Cloud Firestore (Google Firebase), linked to your user ID, so it is available when you sign in. We do not use it for our own analysis and we do not sell it. You can delete each subscription in the app, or request the deletion of your whole account (see below).

B. Automatically Collected Information
When you use SubHunter, we may automatically collect certain information about your device, including:

Device Information: Device model, operating system (Android version), unique device identifiers, and mobile network information.

Usage Data: Details of your use of our application, such as features used and the time spent on the app. This helps us improve the user experience.

C. Permissions
To function correctly, SubHunter requires specific permissions:

Notifications: We request permission to send you push notifications. This is essential for the "aggressive alerts" feature to remind you before a free trial ends or a subscription renews.

